WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.343
This Kotlin function returns a Flow of ledger entries.

2
00:00:06.343 --> 00:00:10.863
Its body asks the ledger service for a page, then emits each entry.

3
00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:13.577
Call it, and nothing happens.

4
00:00:13.577 --> 00:00:15.883
Not one request reaches the ledger.

5
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:19.436
A Flow is a description of the work, like a recipe.

6
00:00:19.436 --> 00:00:22.641
Calling the function only writes the recipe down.

7
00:00:22.867 --> 00:00:24.828
Operators don't run it either.

8
00:00:24.828 --> 00:00:28.621
filter and map take a flow and return a new flow, at once.

9
00:00:28.621 --> 00:00:30.844
They only add steps to the recipe.

10
00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:34.781
Work starts only with a terminal operator, such as collect.

11
00:00:34.781 --> 00:00:40.509
collect is a suspend function, and it runs the body right there, in the caller's coroutine.

12
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:46.698
Each emit pushes one entry through filter and map into your lambda, and waits until that is done.

13
00:00:46.698 --> 00:00:49.339
Only then does the body make the next one.

14
00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:51.257
Now collect a second time.

15
00:00:51.257 --> 00:00:55.937
The body runs again, from the top, and the ledger gets a second request.

16
00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:58.817
That is what cold means.

17
00:00:58.817 --> 00:01:02.924
Every collector gets its own run of the producer, from the start.

18
00:01:03.833 --> 00:01:06.525
A Reactor Flux is cold in the same way.

19
00:01:06.525 --> 00:01:09.009
Nothing happens until you subscribe.

20
00:01:09.233 --> 00:01:14.615
To share one run between collectors, you need a hot flow, StateFlow or SharedFlow.

21
00:01:14.615 --> 00:01:16.649
That is lesson 8 of this track.
